\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 1 \f2\emdash  What Attachment Really Is\par
Key Message\par
Attachment is the bond that tells a child: \ldblquote You are safe with me.\rdblquote\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote Attachment is the emotional connection between you and your child.\par
It\rquote s built through small, everyday moments \emdash  eye contact, warmth, comfort, and presence.\par
When children feel securely attached, they explore, learn, and grow with confidence.\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote Attachment = Safety + Connection\rdblquote\par
\par
Scene Descriptions\par
Parent and child sharing warm eye contact\par
\par
Gentle touch\par
\par
Soft home environment\par
\par
\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 2 \f2\emdash  Secure vs Insecure Attachment\par
Key Message\par
Children behave differently depending on how safe they feel.\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote Secure attachment looks like confidence, curiosity, and trust.\par
Insecure attachment can look like clinginess, avoidance, or confusion.\par
These patterns are not personality \emdash  they are protection.\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote Attachment shapes behaviour.\rdblquote\par
\par
\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 3 \f2\emdash  How Trauma Disrupts Attachment\par
Key Message\par
Trauma teaches children that adults may not be safe.\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote When children experience fear, loss, or inconsistency, their attachment system becomes confused.\par
They may push you away, cling tightly, or shut down.\par
This is not rejection \emdash  it\rquote s protection.\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote Protection, not rejection.\rdblquote\par
\par
\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 4 \f2\emdash  Why Children Test for Safety\par
Key Message\par
Testing is a child\rquote s way of asking: \ldblquote Will you stay?\rdblquote\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote Children who have been hurt often test boundaries, rules, and relationships.\par
They\rquote re not trying to be difficult \emdash  they\rquote re checking if you are safe, consistent, and reliable.\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote Testing = Checking for safety.\rdblquote\par
\par
\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 5 \f2\emdash  Connection Before Correction\par
Key Message\par
Children learn best when they feel connected.\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote Before you correct behaviour, connect emotionally.\par
A child who feels seen and understood is more open to guidance.\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote Connect first. Teach second.\rdblquote\par
\par
\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 6 \f2\emdash  Repairing Attachment Ruptures\par
Key Message\par
Repair matters more than perfection.\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote Every relationship has ruptures \emdash  moments of disconnection.\par
What heals attachment is repair: returning, apologising, reconnecting.\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote Repair > Perfection\rdblquote\par
\par
\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 7 \f2\emdash  Building Trust Through Consistency\par
Key Message\par
Trust grows through repeated safe moments.\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote Children learn to trust when adults show up consistently.\par
Small predictable actions build long\f1\_\f0 term security.\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote Consistency builds trust.\rdblquote\par
\par
\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 8 \f2\emdash  Attachment Through Play\par
Key Message\par
Play is the language of connection.\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote Child\f1\_\f0 led play strengthens attachment.\par
It tells your child: \lquote I enjoy being with you.\rquote\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote Play = Connection\rdblquote\par
\par
\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 9 \f2\emdash  Attachment Through Daily Rituals\par
Key Message\par
Small rituals create big safety.\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote Morning hugs, bedtime stories, shared meals \emdash  these rituals anchor your child\rquote s sense of belonging.\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote Rituals build belonging.\rdblquote\par
\par
\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 10 \f2\emdash  Attachment With Teens\par
Key Message\par
Teens still need connection \emdash  just differently.\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote Teens may pull away, but they still need warmth, presence, and emotional safety.\par
Connection looks like listening, respecting space, and showing up.\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote Teens need connection too.\rdblquote\par
\par
\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 11 \f2\emdash  Attachment When You\rquote re Stressed\par
Key Message\par
Your calm helps your child feel safe.\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote Parenting under stress is hard.\par
Your emotional regulation becomes your child\rquote s emotional anchor.\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote You matter too.\rdblquote\par
\par
\f3\u11088?\f0  EPISODE 12 \f2\emdash  Long\f1\_\f0 Term Attachment Healing\par
Key Message\par
Healing happens through repeated safe moments.\par
\par
Narration\par
\ldblquote Attachment healing is slow, gentle, and built through everyday connection.\par
Every safe moment rewires the brain toward trust.\rdblquote\par
\par
On\f1\_\f0 Screen Text\par
\ldblquote Safety heals.\rdblquote\par
